    "https://wd105.myworkdaysite.com/recruiting/federation/Federation_Careers/job/Wimmera/TAFE-Teacher--Nursing_JR101522": {
      "title": "TAFE Teacher, Nursing",
      "description": "TAFE Teacher, Nursing Skip to main content Federation Careers Sign In Working at Federation Search for Jobs Introduce Yourself TAFE Teacher, Nursing page is loaded TAFE Teacher, Nursing Apply locations Wimmera time type Part time posted on Posted Yesterday time left to apply End Date: November 2, 2026 (15 days left to apply) job requisition id JR101522 Undertake the delivery and assessment of quality TAFE programs, encompassing all facets of the learning cycle. •\tFederation TAFE – Wimmera Campus •\tPart-time (0.6FTE), fixed-term appointment until November 2027 •\tL1.1 to L3.4 range $85,021 - $120,544 (pro rata) p.a. depending on qualifications and experience plus up to 14% superannuation Position closing date: 01/11/2026 Ranked number one university in Australia for First Generation Student Enrolments (Good Universities Guide 2022) and with top rankings in Victoria around student support, social equity, skills and employment, we are driven to make difference to every student and the community providing lifelong learning, skills, and research locally, regionally, and globally. With University and TAFE campuses in Ballarat, Berwick, Gippsland, and the Wimmera we are positioned to provide pathways from vocational education and skills training through to higher education. About the role Federation TAFE is home to vocational education and training delivered by Federation University Australia and offers a broad range of quality education and training programs, reflecting state and national priorities that address the training needs of individuals and industry.  Our TAFE Teachers are responsible for the delivery and assessment of quality vocational education and training (VET) programs.  Encompassing all facets of the learning cycle, the position is required to manage the end-to-end learning process for students from initial enquiry to final assessment using a variety of teaching strategies including recognition of prior learning, online and workplace learning, delivery and assessment as well as traditional classroom delivery. About you Reporting to the Program Manager, you will have the ability to research, develop and implement innovative and appropriate teaching curriculum while effectively utilising online learning platforms and technologies. You will have excellent communication and interpersonal skills and the ability to complete administrative tasks, including the ability to maintain accurate online and physical records. You will: · plan, prepare deliver and assess training programs; · monitor, assess and record student attendance, progress and results; · participate in internal and external contractual audits; and · evaluate student teaching and learning resources. It is a requirement of this position that you hold a Certificate IV in Training and Assessment or a diploma or higher-level qualification in adult education plus current AHPRA registration as a Registered Nurse. All University positions must hold a valid Employer Working With Children Check (WWCC). Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply . How to apply Please apply by Sunday, 1 November 2026 Applicants are required to submit a resume and a response to the key selection criteria. View position description Federation University is committed to The Circle Back Initiative program, whereby we will respond to every applicant. If you are experiencing technical difficulties with your application, please email the Recruitment team or phone 03 5327 9756. Our position descriptions also list a contact person for job specific inquiries. Let our staff tell you more. Similar Jobs (2) TAFE Teacher, Healthcare Industries locations Ballarat, Victoria time type Full time posted on Posted Yesterday time left to apply End Date: November 2, 2026 (15 days left to apply) Casual - TAFE Teacher, Corrections locations Ballarat, Victoria time type Part time posted on Posted 30+ Days Ago time left to apply End Date: January 31, 2027 (30+ days