r learning, online and workplace learning, delivery and assessment as well as traditional classroom delivery. About you Reporting to the Program Manager, you will have the ability to research, develop and implement innovative and appropriate teaching curriculum while effectively utilising online learning platforms and technologies. You will have excellent communication and interpersonal skills and the ability to complete administrative tasks, including the ability to maintain accurate online and physical records. You will: plan, prepare deliver and assess training programs; monitor, assess and record student attendance, progress and results; participate in internal and external contractual audits; and evaluate student teaching and learning resources. It is a requirement of this position that you hold a Certificate IV in Training and Assessment or a diploma or higher-level qualification in adult education plus current AHPRA registration as a Registered Nurse. All University positions must hold a valid Employer Working With Children Check (WWCC). Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply . How to apply Please apply by Sunday, 1 November 2026 Applicants are required to submit a resume and a response to the key selection criteria. View position description Federation University is committed to The Circle Back Initiative program, whereby we will respond to every applicant. If you are experiencing technical difficulties with your application, please email the Recruitment team or phone 03 5327 9756. Our position descriptions also list a contact person for job specific inquiries. Let our staff tell you more. 0:00 / 4:17 About us Established in 1870 Federation University has been reaching communities and building generations of independent thinkers united in the knowledge that they are greater together. Federation University is committed to attracting, developing and retaining the best talent ranging from our academic and research staff to those working in student experience and professional roles. We are all part of a collaborative culture inspiring the highest levels of excellence, innovation, integrity and respect. Read More Follow Us Federation University Information Privacy Procedure © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
