    "https://wd105.myworkdaysite.com/recruiting/federation/Federation_Careers/job/Ballarat-Victoria/Senior-Health--Safety-and-Wellbeing-Advisor_JR101311-1": {
      "title": "Senior Health, Safety and Wellbeing Advisor",
      "description": "Senior Health, Safety and Wellbeing Advisor Skip to main content Federation Careers Sign In Working at Federation Search for Jobs Introduce Yourself Senior Health, Safety and Wellbeing Advisor page is loaded Senior Health, Safety and Wellbeing Advisor Apply locations Ballarat, Victoria time type Full time posted on Posted Yesterday time left to apply End Date: November 2, 2026 (15 days left to apply) job requisition id JR101311 Play a key role in championing and advancing a positive safety and wellbeing culture across the University. •\tPeople and Culture – Mt Helen Campus •\tFull-time, continuing appointment •\tHEW 7 - $104,810 p.a. plus up to 17% superannuation Position closing date: 01/11/2026 Ranked number one university in Australia for First Generation Student Enrolments (Good Universities Guide 2022) and with top rankings in Victoria around student support, social equity, skills and employment, we are driven to make difference to every student and the community providing lifelong learning, skills, and research locally, regionally, and globally. With University and TAFE campuses in Ballarat, Berwick, Gippsland, and the Wimmera we are positioned to provide pathways from vocational education and skills training through to higher education. About the role As the Senior Health, Safety and Wellbeing (HSW) Advisor, you will play a key role in championing and advancing a positive safety and wellbeing culture, while supporting continuous improvement across the University. The role supports leaders, health and safety teams and governance committees to manage health and safety risks, maintain control effectiveness, and produce quality assurance evidence in line with the University’s HSW Governance, Assurance and Enterprise Risk Framework. You will: provide expert health and safety advice across all campuses to support effective OHS strategies, governance, legislative compliance, and continuous improvement; coach, support and advise Health and Safety Implementation Teams (HSITs) and Health and Safety Coordination Teams (HSCTs); identify and analyse data, trends across incidents, hazards, corrective actions and assurance data, distinguishing local issues from systemic risks, and providing clear summaries and briefing materials to inform governance forums; coordinate and undertake regular risk assessments; and collaboratively support and influence committees, providing guidance with assurance, evidence and escalation processes, preparing and synthesising governance materials, and reinforcing clear accountability and decision-making responsibilities. About you Reporting to the Head, Health, Safety and Wellbeing, you will possess proven experience interpreting OHS legislation and applying specialise knowledge to deliver coaching, support and authoritative advice. You will have demonstrated capacity to navigate a large, complex environment with multi-faceted structures and excellent communication and interpersonal skills to address a wide range of stakeholders. You will possess: success in identifying OHS challenges and implementing practical, results-driven solutions across diverse work settings; ability to work autonomously and collaboratively to deliver outcomes within required timeframes; strong analytical, conceptual and problem-solving skills coupled with attention to detail particularly when working with safety systems, data and reporting; experience supporting incident management, injury management and return-to-work processes; and capacity to travel between campuses and to work occasionally outside standard working hours. All University positions must hold a valid Employer Working With Children Check (WWCC). Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people are encouraged to apply How to apply Please apply by Sunday, 1 November 2026 Applicants are required to submit a resume and a response to the key selection criteria. View position description Federation University is committed to The Circle Back Initiative program, whereby we will respond to every applicant. If you are experiencing technical difficulties with your application, please email the Recruitment team or phone 03 5327 9756. Our position descriptions also list a contact person for job specific inquiries. Let our staff tell you more. 0:00 / 4:17 About us Established in 1870 Federation University has been reaching communities and building generations of independent thinkers united in the knowledge that they are greater together. Federation University is committed to attracting, developing and retaining the best talent ranging from our academic and research staff to those working in student experience and professional roles. We are all part of a collaborative culture inspiring the highest levels of excellence, innovation, integrity and respect. Read More Follow Us Federation University Information Privacy Procedure © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
